# Observatory — agent coding rules

Unity-based game platform; first game is The Lost Observatory. Product spec: `game-platform-base-plan_v2.1.md`. Agent workflow: `AGENTS.md`.

Priority order when goals conflict: capacity > foundation > game. Launch stack per v2.1: one production-named Droplet behind basic auth until launch; Compose runs `web`, `api`, `redis`; Keycloak is profile `identity` (off until `/admin/` with operator login exists); Celery/Beat is profile `jobs`, off. Do not enable player login, the `identity` or `jobs` profiles, or multi-tenant abstractions without a named feature.

Do not copy kp-platform rules, Pipenv commands, or GitHub/Revy assumptions.

## Stack (planned)

- `apps/game-unity` — Unity 6.3 LTS (6000.3.x), C#
- `apps/web` — React + TypeScript
- `apps/api` — FastAPI
- Identity — Keycloak at `auth.createit.digital` (Compose profile `identity`, off until a consumer exists)
- Runtime — Docker Compose + host Nginx; DigitalOcean Managed PostgreSQL

Follow lint and tests the repo actually has. Do not invent runners. Manifest `test_commands` is empty until apps exist.

## Collaboration

- Preserve offline play unless a change explicitly modifies that product contract.
- Propose a plan before broad cross-project changes.
- Prefer small, reviewable, reversible changes.
- Do not change identity, production networking, secrets, deployment, or database schema without explicit review.
- Do not put secrets in the Unity client. Do not trust client-submitted competitive, financial, or entitlement state.
- Update tests, documentation, and release notes when behavior or operations change.
- Never overwrite a working scene, asset, or deployment configuration without a Git commit or explicit review point.

## Hosting

Private GitHub `raimondskrauklis/rocky-observatory` (`hosting.kind = github`). Production Revy reviews PRs (same GitHub App as `raimondskrauklis/revy`). Push when the user asks. Do not open a PR unless asked. Never push while Revy is `pending` / `in_progress` / `queued`. Setup: `docs/runbooks/github-revy.md`.
